<title>POLAND: KREDYT BANK TO VOTE ON NEW ISSUE MAY 28.</title>
<headline>KREDYT BANK TO VOTE ON NEW ISSUE MAY 28.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Kredyt Bank SA called a general shareholders meeting for May 28 to vote on a new, ex-rights issue of between 15 million and 25 million common shares of the O series, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the new issue would raise Kredyt Bank's capital by 75 million to 125 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Shareholders will also vote on Kredyt Bank's 1996 dividend. The bank now has 25,631,304 shares outstanding. It traded at 8.45 zlotys at the last bourse session on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
